00:36:18,040 --> 00:36:22,360
 initially and you know good centers initially.

389
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:27,680
 So we will be spending some time on this particular aspect and see what we can do to tackle this

390
00:36:27,680 --> 00:36:31,960
 particular problem.

391
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:38,800
 So some of the consequences of this initial center something like that you can have slow

392
00:36:38,800 --> 00:36:44,840
 convergence that means it can take a lot of time to reach to a point where you can see

393
00:36:44,840 --> 00:36:50,520
 that you know my clusters are good or you converge to a suboptimal clustering that means

394
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:56,880
 the quality of cluster is actually very bad that means the clusters are dispersed okay.

395
00:36:56,880 --> 00:37:05,960
 So to tackle this problem in literature you have a load of common heuristics that people

396
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:08,480
 generally adopt okay.

397
00:37:08,480 --> 00:37:17,680
 So we do random centers in the space, we randomly pick from the future vectors, we choose points

