00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:22,680
 use of which we call first center then for the remaining points we find out that which

409
00:38:22,680 --> 00:38:27,840
 point is furthest from the existing point that we have already chosen okay.

410
00:38:27,840 --> 00:38:32,560
 The one which has the highest distance from the existing points will choose that as a

411
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:36,560
 potential centroid and you simply move on like that one.

412
00:38:36,560 --> 00:38:42,040
 So objective is to make sure that the points which are far apart in the original data will

413
00:38:42,040 --> 00:38:51,320
 be chosen as possible possibly good initial centroids but it has its own problem.

